at the opening of his trial in lüneburg  the former Nazi SS guard asked for  forgiveness I share morally in the guilt  oscar guling told the court the 93 year  old admits that he had learned jews were  being killed shortly after his arrival  at auschwitz concentration camp  the prosecution accuses him of accessory  to murder in the deaths of at least  300,000 people as an active member of  the vafan SS the defendant is said to  have taken the money of prisoners in the  camp he's alleged to have counted the  banknotes in the luggage of newly  arrived detainees and forwarded the  money to SS headquarters in Berlin  joining is said to have asked three  times for a transfer out of Auschwitz  his defense maintains he's not guilty  legally this process is very difficult  because individual guilt must always be  established in addition there's the  moral aspect that's undisputed and  that's something that should be  discussed at a different level more than  60 Auschwitz survivors and relatives of  the victims have come from around the  world to attend the proceedings if Oskar  Gruening is found guilty and declared  fit for prison he faces at least three  years behind bars
 

